  upd_title:'New version available',upd_body:'Tap to load the latest build.',upd_btn:'Update',upd_later:'Later',
  pwa_title:'Install Heimdall',pwa_body:'Add it to your home screen: full screen, one tap, no browser bar.',pwa_btn:'Install',pwa_no:'Not now',
  pwa_ios:'On iPhone: tap the Share button, then "Add to Home Screen".',
  m_help:'How this app works',m_support:'Support the project',m_lite:'Blackout mode (2G / weak signal)',
  help_title:'How Heimdall works',
  help_intro:'The app reads public sources every few seconds — the Air Force, oblast and city administrations, volunteer monitoring channels, the official alert feeds — and draws what they reported on one map. It never invents anything: every marker can be traced back to the sentence it came from.',
  help_warn:'This is not an official warning system. Always rely on city sirens and the official «Air Raid Alert» app; if an alert sounds, proceed to shelter immediately.',
  h1_t:'The status band',h1_b:'The top band follows the oblast you chose. Red means an air raid alert, yellow a yellow-level alert, green all clear, with how long it has been running. The whole oblast is painted whenever the state declares an oblast-wide alert, exactly as the government app shows it.',
  h2_t:'The map',h2_b:'All 27 oblasts and 136 raions are coloured by their alert level. Tap an oblast to see its towns. Zoom in past 150 km and streets and buildings appear. Kyiv has its own simplified map of the 10 districts — open it from the menu.',
  h3_t:'Targets',h3_b:'Shaheds are drawn circling the point where they were reported, because their real path is erratic — the chevron shows the heading someone reported, not a course line. Missiles are red, jet drones lighter orange, KABs violet. A number badge means several targets reported at the same place.',
  h4_t:'Why a target is never a straight arrow',h4_b:'Nobody publishes radar tracks. Drawing a trajectory would imply a precision that does not exist, and no arrival time is ever shown. If you want to see an estimate of motion along the reported heading, switch on EST in the menu — it is off by default and clearly labelled.',
  h5_t:'Grey targets with a “?”',h5_b:'No new report for 5 minutes and the target turns grey, stops moving and says how long it has been silent. It fades step by step and disappears after 15 minutes. Grey means "this is the last thing anyone said", not "it is still there".',
  h6_t:'Descending targets',h6_b:'When a post says a drone is descending — знижується — the marker shows ↓ DESCENDING. That is the moment it dives on its target. Altitude in metres is shown only when the post states it; no source publishes altitude, so nothing is ever guessed.',
  h7_t:'Tap any target',h7_b:'You get the original sentence, the channel, the time, how the position, heading and count were read, the confidence of each, and other reports nearby. If a value has no evidence behind it, it is not shown.',
  h8_t:'The warning banner',h8_b:'A MiG-31K take-off or a ballistic threat raises a banner before anything is seen, and it disappears as soon as a post lifts it. A nightly threat assessment ("threats are above average tonight") is a forecast and never raises it.',
  h9_t:'History and statistics',h9_b:'The ✸ button cycles through explosions and confirmed shoot-downs over 24 / 48 / 72 hours. The Stats tab has alerts per day and by time of day, and what the Air Force reported as launched over Ukraine — kept separate from the number of monitoring posts, which counts reports, not targets.',
  h10_t:'Notifications',h10_b:'Push notifications reach your phone with the app closed. Set a priority place, or allow your location and choose a radius to be warned when something is reported within it. On iPhone, add the app to your home screen first.',
  h11_t:'Blackout mode',h11_b:'For 2G or a weak signal during an attack: pure black and white, no map tiles, no images, minimal data. Everything essential stays — alerts, targets, distances.',
  h12_t:'Languages',h12_b:'English, Ukrainian and French, switchable at any time from the menu or the flags on the welcome screen. Posts themselves stay in the original Ukrainian or machine-translated English.',
  sup_title:'Support Heimdall',
  sup_body:'The app is free and stays free. If it is useful to you, a donation covers the server, the development and the humanitarian work of NGO 07300 — and supports the person building it.',
  sup_how:'Send a donation to',sup_copy:'Copy',sup_copied:'Copied',sup_thanks:'Thank you — it genuinely keeps this running.',sup_never:'Never show this again',
  sup_hint:'The service is completely free. Any support for hosting, development and the NGO “07300 — People for People” is sincerely appreciated.',
  flag_btn:'⚑ Wrong?',flag_title:'⚑ Report a wrong reading',flag_sub:'What is wrong with this marker? It changes nothing on the map — it files the post for review, so the same misreading can be fixed and tested against.',flag_place:'Wrong place',flag_type:'Wrong type of threat',flag_nothreat:'Not a threat at all — news, an announcement, a press release',flag_gone:'Already gone / already shot down',flag_other:'Something else',flag_note:'Anything to add (optional)',flag_send:'Send',flag_thanks:'Filed — thank you. Nothing on the map changed.',flag_fail:'Could not send it. It needs a connection.',share_btn:'Share',share_copied:'Copied to clipboard',
  share_foot:'Position from a public post, not radar. Follow the official alerts.',
