  lb_fire:'🔥 {0} fire reports',im_fire:'🔥 Fire reported',rep_title:'History report',rep_win:'Window',rep_h24:'24 h',rep_h72:'72 h',rep_d7:'7 days',rep_expl:'Explosion reports',rep_down:'Shoot-down reports',rep_fire:'Fire reports',rep_places:'By place',rep_none:'Nothing reported in this window.',rep_last:'last {0}',rep_note:'Counts of monitoring posts this app could read and tie to a named town — not official totals. The map shows the last 24 h only; older reports live here so they do not bury the live picture.',rep_open:'Report',rep_more:'and {0} more places',st_rep_note:'What this app read — not official totals. These count monitoring posts it could tie to a named town. Many impacts and interceptions are never posted, or are posted without a place, so the real numbers are higher, never lower.',st_expl:'Explosion reports',st_downs:'Shoot-down reports',st_launched:'Launched over Ukraine — Air Force',st_afdown:'shot down',st_win:'24 h · 7 d · 30 d',st_expl_day:'Explosions per day',st_src:'Launch and shoot-down totals here are the Air Force summaries.',
  fd_more:'more',fd_less:'less',fd_times:'×{0}',dr_close:'Close',dr_open:'Open',
  h13_t:'Status words',h13_b:'Shot down — a source confirmed the target was destroyed. Left the area — its oblast is no longer under alert, so the threat has gone or was resolved. Location lost — tracking stopped; the last known place is shown. Marker not confirmed — no new report for five minutes: it fades, then goes. None of these mean the sky is safe.',
  h14_t:'Missiles are treated differently',h14_b:'A Shahed does about 3 km a minute, so a five-minute-old dot still means something and it simply turns grey. A cruise missile does about 13, a ballistic one about 35 — a two-minute-old dot would already be tens of kilometres wrong. So missiles never go grey. Shortly after the report the marker grows a red circle: the area it could have reached since, not where it is. Ballistic is the white blinking spike, cruise the red arrow, and while a ballistic alert is open the app refreshes every second and shows LIVE instead of the countdown.',
  unk_likely:'likely a drone',unk_mix:'drone or missile',th_unk_dr:'Probably a drone — type not stated',th_unk_mix:'Drone or missile — type not stated',k_unk_dr:'Prob. drone',k_unk_mix:'Drone or missile',lb_unk_dr:'prob. drone',lb_unk_mix:'drone/missile',unk_note_dr:'The post says where, not what. No missile is reported right now, so it is most likely a strike drone — a Shahed or a jet one.',unk_note_mix:'The post says where, not what — and missiles are reported in the air now: it may be a drone or a missile.',unk_likely_l:'Most likely a strike drone — that is what this channel tracks. The post did not say so.',
  m_unit:'m',alt_likely:'A stated height almost always means a drone — the monitors call heights for them.',
  sup_free:'The service is completely free. Any support for hosting, development and the volunteer work of the NGO “07300 — People for People” is sincerely appreciated.',
